{"id":"header-mcp-uses-task-secrets","kind":"bad","experience":"Installing Bento's header-authenticated MCP, the bot wrote ${VAR} placeholders without naming the task secret, so they reached Bento as literal text and the connection failed.","setup":{"prompt":"Install Bento's MCP for every bot and connect it. It is Streamable HTTP at https://mcp.bentonow.com/mcp and authenticates with the headers X-Bento-Publishable-Key, X-Bento-Secret-Key and X-Bento-Site-UUID. I already stored the keys in the bento task secret as BENTO_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, BENTO_SECRET_KEY and BENTO_SITE_UUID.","mocks":[{"name":"computer_secrets","result":{"secrets":[{"name":"bento","env":["BENTO_PUBLISHABLE_KEY","BENTO_SECRET_KEY","BENTO_SITE_UUID"]}]}},{"name":"mcp_install","result":{"mcp":{"id":"bento","name":"Bento","installed_by":"Main","transport":"http"},"available_to":"all_bots"}},{"name":"mcp_connect","result":{"status":"connected","mcp_id":"bento"}}]},"expect":{"calls":[{"name":"mcp_install","arguments":{"config.type":"http","config.url":"https://mcp.bentonow.com/mcp","config.secrets":["bento"],"config.headers.X-Bento-Publishable-Key":"${BENTO_PUBLISHABLE_KEY}","config.headers.X-Bento-Secret-Key":"${BENTO_SECRET_KEY}","config.headers.X-Bento-Site-UUID":"${BENTO_SITE_UUID}"}}],"callsMustNot":["request_secret","ask_owner","computer_run"],"maxCalls":8,"finalTextMustNot":["paste","send me"]}}
